{
 "about": "Figures of merit of DESI C_gg alone when the bias parameters are untied per bin, relative to the summary model. Model (fom_model, fom_om_as_model): model B + tilts (notes/higher_order_bias: offsets and counterterms per group with a straight line in redshift, flat priors on the tilts, SN0 and SN2 per group) on the pessimistic linear-bias prior, DESI C_gg alone, against the scale cut k_max [h/Mpc; the z = 0 value of a per-bin cut at k_max/D(zbar_i), D the growth factor, by the UV-fraction criterion, alpha = 0.05, within the shipped mask]; null where a cut leaves no fit. Written by EXAMPLE_EVALUATE_FISHER_MODEL_B.ipynb. Versions, each with b1 free per bin (flat prior) and one value per bin of Delta_2, Delta_s, alpha_0, alpha_2, SN0 and SN2: gauss = each per-bin parameter with the width w the model gives its group, no group offsets, no tilts; sqrtn = width w sqrt(N_g), N_g the number of bins of the group in the layout; sqrtn_tilt = the same plus a flat tilt in redshift per group for Delta_2, Delta_s, alpha_0 and alpha_2; nested = per-bin parameters of width w on top of the model's group offsets and tilts. fom and fom_om_as: per version and cut; ratio_fom and ratio_fom_om_as: version / model. FoM(w0, wa) and FoM(Omega_m, 10^9 A_s) are each det(marginalized 2x2 covariance)^(-1/2).",
